```rust
pub trait CapacityProvider: Send + Sync + 'static {
    /// Maximum number of requests allowed in flight right now.
    fn max_in_flight(&self) -> usize;
}
```

The fairshare scheduler calls this every time it considers granting a permit. The result is a **total ceiling summed across every model's pool** (see [Fairshare Engine](/docs/concepts/fairshare-engine)) — it is not a fairness input and does not decide which model, tenant, or key a slot goes to. It only stops aggregate in-flight requests from exceeding what you configure. When it binds, pools are served round-robin rather than by weight.

The `Tokenizer` trait in `obleth-tokenizer` is the seam:

```rust
pub trait Tokenizer: Send + Sync {
    fn count_text(&self, text: &str) -> u32;
    fn estimate_request(&self, body: &Value) -> CostEstimate { ... }
}
```

Drop in a `tiktoken-rs` or HuggingFace `tokenizers` implementation for model-accurate counting without changing anything else in the pipeline.

Serve a JSON document, unauthenticated, at a stable URL. Every key needs a
`kid`, because the gateway looks keys up by `kid` alone and skips entries
without one, logging a warning as it loads the document.

```json
{
  "keys": [
    {
      "kty": "EC",
      "crv": "P-256",
      "alg": "ES256",
      "use": "sig",
      "kid": "2026-09-a",
      "x": "…base64url…",
      "y": "…base64url…"
    }
  ]
}
```

Node can derive the `x`/`y` pair from the public PEM directly, which avoids
transcribing them by hand:

```js
import { createPublicKey } from "node:crypto";
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";

const jwk = createPublicKey(readFileSync("signing-key.pub.pem")).export({
  format: "jwk",
});
console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...jwk, alg: "ES256", use: "sig", kid: "2026-09-a" }));
```

Any stable string works as a `kid` as long as it changes when the key does; a
date-stamped label is enough. This endpoint is public by design — it contains
only public keys, and the gateway fetches it without credentials.

Retrieval never fails a request. Each of these leaves the request exactly as it
arrived:

- the boon is disabled, not granted, or the model has no attached collection;
- no user text to build a query from, or the model has no context window
  configured;
- the embedding model is unregistered, has no reachable endpoint, errors, or
  times out;
- the attached collections are empty or not yet indexed;
- nothing scores above `min_score`, or nothing fits the token budget.

Query embeddings are not billed to the tenant and do not count against term
budgets.

