For Claude Code and the Anthropic SDKs, see
[Claude Code & Anthropic SDKs](/docs/guides/anthropic-messages-api).

```bash
curl -s http://localhost:8088/v1/verdicts \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $SECRET" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "qwen3-8b",
    "state": {"ticket": "My card was charged twice for order A-104. Please refund the duplicate."},
    "questions": {
      "is_urgent": {
        "type": "boolean",
        "instructions": "Does this need action today?",
        "criteria": {
          "true": "Time-sensitive: money, security, outage",
          "false": "Routine; can wait for the normal queue"
        }
      },
      "department": {
        "type": "choice",
        "instructions": "Which team should handle this?",
        "criteria": {
          "billing": "Payments, refunds, invoices",
          "technical": "Bugs, errors, outages",
          "account": "Login, profile, access"
        }
      },
      "frustration": {
        "type": "score",
        "instructions": "How frustrated is the customer?",
        "criteria": ["Calm and factual", "Mildly annoyed", "Frustrated", "Very angry"]
      }
    }
  }'
```

| Field | Type | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `model` | string | A registered chat model name or alias, or `auto` |
| `state` | string, object, or array | The content to evaluate. Structured values are rendered as pretty-printed JSON |
| `questions` | object | Question id to question. Each question has a `type` and `instructions` |

`instructions` and every criteria description accept a string or structured
JSON; objects and arrays a

```json
{
  "model": "qwen3-8b",
  "verdicts": {
    "department": {
      "type": "choice",
      "value": "billing",
      "probabilities": {"account": 0.0007, "billing": 0.9962, "technical": 0.0031},
      "confidence": 0.97
    },
    "frustration": {
      "type": "score",
      "value": 2,
      "probabilities": [0.11, 0.78, 0.09, 0.02],
      "confidence": 0.62,
      "expected_value": 2.02
    },
    "is_urgent": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "value": true,
      "probabilities": {"false": 0.06, "true": 0.94},
      "confidence": 0.71
    }
  },
  "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 430, "completion_tokens": 3, "total_tokens": 433}
}
```

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `model` | The canonical model name that served the request (aliases and `auto` resolved) |
| `type` | The question type |
| `value` | The argmax: the single answer you would act on |
| `probabilities` | The model's distribution over the answer labels, renormalized to sum to 1. For `score` it is an array in level order, because object keys would sort `"10"` before `"2"` |
| `confidence` | How decisively the model answered, from 0 to 1 (see below) |
| `expected_value` | `score` only: the probability-weighted level, `Σ pᵢ · levelᵢ`, a smoother signal than the argmax when adjacent levels split the mass |
| `usage` | Token totals summed across every question's calls, including retries |

`server` is the registered MCP server name from the `/mcp/<server>` path;
`status` is the status class. See
[Data Plane Routes](/docs/reference/data-plane-routes#mcp-gateway).
